Hey everyone, we&#8217;re excited to share news on Gran Turismo with you today. For starters, we have full details on today&#8217;s Part 1 of the Gran Turismo 7 Spec IV update. Plus, we celebrate 30 years of Gran Turismo with the first look at the Gran Turismo Limited Edition DualSense wireless controller! Read on for full details.
Gran Turismo 7 Spec IV Update (Part 1) &#8211; out today&nbsp;&nbsp;
Today, all players will receive Part 1 of the Gran Turismo 7 Spec IV update. Whether you&#8217;re chasing lap times, discovering automotive history, capturing the perfect photo, building your dream collection, or simply looking for something new to drive, Spec IV adds new ways to explore the world of cars with six new vehicles, the Sportsland Sugo circuit, new events, Scapes locations, gameplay features, and more.&nbsp;
Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo is an electric hypercar sculpted by the wind. Its teardrop-shaped cockpit is embedded within a body sculpted with cutouts and air ducts, forming aerodynamic channels throughout the vehicle. The signature halo-shaped taillight serves as both a visual icon and a massive air outlet.&nbsp;
&#8220;Electric hypercars must answer a fundamental question,&#8221; said Tianyuan Li, Design Head of Xiaomi Auto. &#8220;Do we pursue extreme low drag for straight-line speed, or maximum downforce to conquer corners? The optimal solution lies in finding the perfect balance between the two.&#8221; This approach impressed Gran Turismo Series Producer Kazunori Yamauchi. &#8220;When I saw that Xiaomi had resolved the contradiction between low drag and high downforce, I was truly amazed.&#8221; &nbsp;
Try this in GT7: Take it to the Spa-Francorchamps circuit in the Vision Gran Turismo Trophy event and see how its futuristic design translates to one of racing&#8217;s most historic circuits. &nbsp;&nbsp;
The Mugen Motul Civic, which won the overall class victory at the 1987 All-Japan Touring Car Championship, was a Group A race car developed from the twin-cam &#8216;Si&#8217; model that joined the 3rd generation Civic line-up in 1984. The Civic Si Group A version featured in Gran Turismo is based on this Mugen Motul Civic. &nbsp;

